parts.append('''<h2 id="missing">Completeness has several meanings</h2><p>The selected 16 fields produce 384 record–field pairs. Of 242 structural absences, 144 are named by at least one completeness comment and 98 are not. These counts describe reviewer attention to selected structural gaps; they do not estimate recall because applicability and source-supported expected content were not established.</p><p><strong>Important correction to a tempting interpretation:</strong> download_url is defined in the historical schema as a URL pointing directly to the data, distinct from a landing page. Its absence should not automatically be “fixed” by inserting FAIRhub or Dataverse access pages. In S19, the access route is already structured under distribution_formats.access_urls.</p>''');fig('15_structural_absence')
parts.append('''<p>Evidence examples distinguish several levels: S01/S19 have an access route elsewhere; S25 contains a selective variable summary plus referenced dictionaries; S05’s source explicitly says no DPIA was conducted but the dedicated D4D field is empty; S31 records the same kind of negative declaration in a populated field. These should not all receive the same completeness interpretation.</p><p><a href="data/followup/field_presence.json">All 384 record–field observations</a> · <a href="data/followup/historical_schema_evidence.json">Historical schema evidence</a></p><h2 id="agreement">Scores, flagged fields, and recurring concerns</h2>''');fig('16_agreement')
