for p,v in S['repeat_summary'].items():parts.append(f'<tr><td>{p}</td><td>{v["score_range_pp"]:.1f}</td><td>{v["mean_field_jaccard"]:.1%}</td><td>{v["mean_typed_jaccard"]:.1%}</td></tr>')
parts.append('''</table><p>Low cross-rubric overlap is not automatically poor reliability: the instruments ask different questions. Repeat-review overlap is more directly relevant to evaluator stability, but covers only four fixed records and still spans documented execution changes.</p>''');fig('23_recurring_topics');fig('19_signature_counts')
parts.append(f'<p>Strict signature grouping reduces 562 comment entries to {S["strict_signature_total"]} record-specific signatures; the broader definition yields {S["broad_signature_total"]}. This small reduction shows that exact field-set matching is too conservative to serve as a complete semantic deduplication. The selected-topic figure is a readable complement, not a claim that we have counted distinct errors.</p><p><a href="data/followup/cross_rubric_agreement.json">Cross-rubric overlap details</a> · <a href="data/followup/repeat_agreement.json">Repeat pairs</a> · <a href="data/followup/topic_rules.json">Topic rules</a> · <a href="data/followup/topic_assignments.json">Topic assignments</a> · <a href="data/followup/field_topic_signatures.json">Grouped signatures</a></p>')
