parts.append('</table><p>Removing Q19 changes AI_READI’s contrast from −1.14 to −0.40 points, while CM4AI remains about −5.6 points. Removing both Q13 and Q19 makes CM4AI’s contrast more negative (−7.33 points), partly because this is a different score subset and denominator. The original exploratory tests and their multiple-comparison adjustments remain unchanged; no new significance claim is made.</p>');fig('18_denominator_effect')
parts.append('<details><summary>Item distributions and ceiling effects</summary>');fig('20_item_distributions');parts.append('</details><p><a href="data/followup/score_sensitivity.json">Per-record diagnostic scores</a> · <a href="data/followup/score_sensitivity_summary.json">Version contrasts</a> · <a href="data/followup/item_score_distribution.json">Item counts</a></p>')
parts.append('''<h2 id="evidence">Evidence review of 32 comments</h2><p>Sampling used seed 20260930 and selected one primary comment per dataset × rubric × review family. Correctness and content_accuracy form one family. Within each stratum selection was uniform from issue IDs sorted lexically. The result is balanced over those strata, not over severity or population frequency. This sample contains no high-severity comments; it cannot characterize the most severe issues. The sampling probabilities and stratum sizes are retained.</p>''');fig('22_sample_dispositions')
counts=collections.Counter(a['primary_disposition'] for a in A);parts.append('<table><tr><th>Primary disposition</th><th>Sample comments</th><th>Interpretation</th></tr>')
why={'Representation / selective summary':'Content exists elsewhere, coverage is selective, or the concern is classification/readability. Not necessarily an inaccurate result.','Documented source differences':'Source wording, dates, units, or roles differ; the D4D often preserves the distinction.','Documentation gap; provenance unresolved':'A D4D gap is supported, but whether the source corpus allowed it to be filled remains unsettled.','Explicit source limitation':'The source explicitly says an assessment was not done; documentation fidelity and underlying practice are separate.','Reviewer claim overstated or contradicted':'At least one allegation conflicts with the record/schema or overinterprets a source convention; mixed components remain.','Inherited wording or citation convention':'The questionable string or format comes from the source or its recommended citation.','Generated scope ambiguity':'The generated wording insufficiently separates release scope from project or companion-dataset context.'}
for c,n in counts.items():parts.append(f'<tr><td>{c}</td><td>{n}</td><td>{why[c]}</td></tr>')
parts.append('''</table><h3>Concrete corrections and proposed clarifications</h3><ul><li><strong>Analysis framing:</strong> replace any shorthand “18 missing download URLs” with “18 records had a completeness comment naming an absent download_url; the field is structurally absent in all 24.”</li><li><strong>Evaluator claim, S30:</strong> bare doi plus CURIE id conforms to the historical schema; split off the separate publisher-field concern.</li><li><strong>Evaluator claim, S12:</strong> the record explicitly distinguishes the software MIT license from the data’s access agreement. Preserve the narrower missing-license-detail concern.</li><li><strong>Evaluator claims, S22/S24:</strong> distinguish separate Dataverse deposits and the source’s own V2/2.0 display conventions.</li><li><strong>D4D wording, S32:</strong> describe four adult disease categories plus controls in the adult-release paragraph; identify pediatric data as a separate companion release.</li><li><strong>D4D wording, S20:</strong> mark the three-condition AP-MS description as preprint/project context, then state the current release’s treated-condition scope.</li></ul><p>These are proposed interpretation and wording corrections. No source D4D or original score was edited. The case table below preserves the original comment, evidence, proposed action, and uncertainty.</p><input id="casefilter" placeholder="Search cases: DOI, license, source limitation, S32…" aria-label="Filter evidence cases"><p id="casecount" class="small">32 cases</p>''')
for a in A:
 ev=json.loads((D/a['evidence_file']).read_text());sid=a['sample_id'];parts.append(f'<section class="case" id="{sid}"><h3>{sid} · {a["record"]} · rubric{a["rubric"]}</h3><span class="pill">{a["primary_disposition"]}</span><p class="small">Original label: {a["type"]}; severity: {a["severity"]}. Issue {a["issue_id"]}. Stratum size: {a["stratum_size"]}.</p><blockquote>{esc(a["description"])}</blockquote><p><strong>Assessment:</strong> {esc(a["assessment"])}</p><p><strong>Action:</strong> {esc(a["recommended_action"])}</p><p><strong>Uncertainty:</strong> {esc(a["uncertainty"])}</p><details><summary>Record and source evidence</summary><p class="small">D4D SHA-256: {ev["d4d_sha256"]}. <a href="data/followup/{a["evidence_file"]}">Full evidence JSON</a>. Source snippets come from recovered historical chunks; searches were targeted, not exhaustive.</p><pre>{esc(json.dumps(ev["d4d_fields"],indent=2))}</pre>')
